    ('---\nname: typefully\nversion: 1.0.0\ndescription: |\n  Schedule and manage Twitter/X and LinkedIn posts via Typefully API.\n  Compose tweets, threads, schedule posts, view drafts, check queue, and pull analytics.\n  Use /typefully to start.\nallowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - AskUserQuestion\n---\n\n# Typefully: Schedule & Manage Social Posts\n\nYou are running the `/typefully` skill. This lets the user compose, schedule, and manage Twitter/X and LinkedIn posts via the Typefully API v2.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe API key is stored in the macOS Keychain. Read it at runtime:\n\n```bash\nKEY=$(security find-generic-password -a "typefully" -s "typefully-api-key" -w 2>/dev/null)\n```\n\nIf the key is not found, print this setup message and STOP:\n\n> **Typefully API key not found in Keychain.**\n>\n> 1. Get your API key from [Typefully Settings](https://typefully.com/settings)\n> 2. Run this command in Terminal:\n>    ```\n>    security add-generic-password -a "typefully" -s "typefully-api-key" -w "YOUR_API_KEY" -U\n>    ```\n> 3. Then re-run `/typefully`\n\n## Arguments & Subcommands\n\nParse arguments from the user\'s invocation. Supported forms:\n\n| Invocation | Action |\n|------------|--------|\n| `/typefully` | Interactive mode — ask what they want to do |\n| `/typefully schedule "tweet text"` | Schedule a single post to next queue slot |\n| `/typefully schedule "text" --at "2026-03-18T10:00:00Z"` | Schedule at a specific time |\n| `/typefully schedule "text" --platform x` | Post to X only (default: both X and LinkedIn) |\n| `/typefully schedule "text" --platform linkedin` | Post to LinkedIn only |\n| `/typefully thread "post 1" \\| "post 2" \\| "post 3"` | Schedule a thread (pipe-separated posts) |\n| `/typefully drafts` | List recent drafts |\n| `/typefully drafts --status scheduled` | List drafts filtered by status |\n| `/typefully queue` | Show upcoming queue for next 7 days |\n| `/typefully accounts` | List connected social sets |\n| `/typefully analytics` | Show post analytics for last 7 days |\n| `/typefully analytics --days 30` | Show analytics for custom period |\n| `/typefully delete <draft_id>` | Delete a draft (asks for confirmation) |\n| `/typefully setup` | Print setup instructions |\n\n## API Base URL\n\n```\nhttps://api.typefully.com\n```\n\nAll requests require:\n- `Authorization: Bearer $KEY`\n- `Content-Type: application/json`\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Step 0: Auth Check\n\nEvery invocation starts by reading the key:\n\n```bash\nKEY=$(security find-generic-password -a "typefully" -s "typefully-api-key" -w 2>/dev/null)\nif [ -z "$KEY" ]; then\n  echo "KEY_NOT_FOUND"\nfi\n```\n\nIf `KEY_NOT_FOUND`, print the setup message above and stop.\n\n### Step 1: Resolve Social Set\n\nFetch the user\'s social sets to get the `social_set_id`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nResponse is paginated: `{ results: [...], count, limit, offset }`.\nEach result has: `id`, `name`, connected platform info.\n\n- If only one social set exists, use it automatically.\n- If multiple exist, present a numbered list and ask which to use via AskUserQuestion.\n- Cache the chosen `social_set_id` in a shell variable for subsequent calls in the session.\n\n### Step 2: Execute Subcommand\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `schedule`\n\nCreates a draft with optional scheduling.\n\n**Default behavior:** Posts to BOTH X and LinkedIn unless `--platform` restricts it.\n\n### Build the request body:\n\nFor a single post (both platforms):\n```json\n{\n  "platforms": {\n    "x": {\n      "enabled": true,\n      "posts": [{ "text": "The tweet text" }]\n    },\n    "linkedin": {\n      "enabled": true,\n      "posts": [{ "text": "The tweet text" }]\n    }\n  },\n  "publish_at": "2026-03-18T10:00:00Z"\n}\n```\n\n- **IMPORTANT:** Only include platforms that are enabled. Do NOT send a platform with `enabled: false` — omit it entirely from the `platforms` object. The API rejects disabled platforms with posts.\n- If `--platform x`, only include the `x` key in `platforms`.\n- If `--platform linkedin`, only include the `linkedin` key in `platforms`.\n- Omit `publish_at` to add to the next available queue slot.\n- If `--at` is provided, use it as `publish_at` (ISO 8601 format).\n\n### Make the API call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$SOCIAL_SET_ID/drafts" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \\\n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n  -d "$BODY"\n```\n\n### Report result:\n\nOn success, show:\n- Draft ID\n- Scheduled time (or "queued for next slot")\n- Platforms enabled\n- Preview of the text\n\nOn error, show the error message from the API response.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `thread`\n\nSame as `schedule` but with multiple posts. The user separates posts with `|`.\n\nSplit the input on `|`, trim whitespace, and build the posts array:\n\n```json\n{\n  "platforms": {\n    "x": {\n      "enabled": true,\n      "posts": [\n        { "text": "First tweet" },\n        { "text": "Second tweet" },\n        { "text": "Third tweet" }\n      ]\n    },\n    "linkedin": {\n      "enabled": true,\n      "posts": [\n        { "text": "First tweet" },\n        { "text": "Second tweet" },\n        { "text": "Third tweet" }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nShow a preview of the thread before posting and ask for confirmation via AskUserQuestion.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `drafts`\n\nList recent drafts.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$SOCIAL_SET_ID/drafts?limit=10&order_by=-updated_at" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nOptional filter: `--status` (draft, published, scheduled, error, publishing).\n\nIf status is specified, add `&status=<value>` to the query.\n\nDisplay as a table:\n\n| ID | Status | Scheduled | Preview | Platforms |\n|----|--------|-----------|---------|-----------|\n\nTruncate preview text to 60 characters.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `queue`\n\nShow the upcoming queue.\n\n```bash\nSTART=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\nEND=$(date -u -v+7d +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\ncurl -s "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$SOCIAL_SET_ID/queue?start_date=$START&end_date=$END" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nDisplay slots with their times and any assigned drafts.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `accounts`\n\nList social sets:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nDisplay as a table: ID, Name, Connected Platforms.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `analytics`\n\nFetch analytics for X posts (currently the only platform supported by the API).\n\n```bash\nSTART=$(date -u -v-7d +%Y-%m-%d)\nEND=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)\ncurl -s "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$SOCIAL_SET_ID/analytics/x/posts?start_date=$START&end_date=$END&limit=25" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nIf `--days N` is provided, adjust `START` to N days ago.\n\nDisplay as a table:\n\n| Post | Date | Impressions | Likes | Comments | Shares | Link Clicks |\n|------|------|-------------|-------|----------|--------|-------------|\n\nTruncate post preview to 50 characters. Show totals row at bottom.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `delete`\n\nDelete a draft by ID. ALWAYS ask for confirmation first via AskUserQuestion.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X DELETE "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$SOCIAL_SET_ID/drafts/$DRAFT_ID" \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"\n```\n\nExpects 204 No Content on success.\n\n---\n\n## Subcommand: `setup`\n\nPrint the setup instructions (same as the auth-not-found message).\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\nAPI errors return:\n```json\n{\n  "error": {\n    "code": "ERROR_CODE",\n    "message": "Human-readable message",\n    "details": [{"field": "...", "message": "..."}]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCommon codes:\n- `UNAUTHORIZED` — bad API key, prompt to re-run setup\n- `RATE_LIMITED` — show reset time from headers\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` — show field-level details\n- `FORBIDDEN` — insufficient permissions on the social set\n- `NOT_FOUND` — bad draft/social set ID\n\nAlways check HTTP status code. On non-2xx, parse and display the error.\n\n## Rate Limit Awareness\n\nAfter each API call, check these response headers:\n- `X-RateLimit-User-Remaining`\n- `X-RateLimit-User-Reset`\n\nIf remaining < 5, warn: "Rate limit low: N requests remaining, resets at TIME."\n\n## Important Rules\n\n1. **Never hardcode the API key** — always read from Keychain at runtime.\n2. **Confirm before publishing** — for `schedule` and `thread`, show a preview and ask "Post this?" via AskUserQuestion before making the API call.\n3. **All curl commands must use `-s` (silent)** to suppress progress output.\n4. **Chain KEY read + curl in a single Bash call** so the key only exists in that shell process.\n5. **Combine key retrieval and API call** in one Bash invocation:\n   ```bash\n   KEY=$(security find-generic-password -a "typefully" -s "typefully-api-key" -w 2>/dev/null) && \\\n   curl -s -X POST "https://api.typefully.com/v2/social-sets/$ID/drafts" \\\n     -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \\\n     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n     -d \'...\'\n   ```\n6. **Parse JSON responses with jq** if available, otherwise use python3 -c for JSON parsing.\n7. **Dates must be ISO 8601** format for the API.\n8. **Default platforms are X + LinkedIn** unless `--platform` overrides.\n', True),
